&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The Client Service team connects&amp;nbsp;Guidepoint’s&amp;nbsp;clients with subject-matter experts to better&amp;nbsp;inform&amp;nbsp;their business decisions. They take the time to understand each client’s specific research needs and deliver the experts closest to the topic, often within hours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play a vital role in Guidepoint’s success.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As an Associate on the Client Service team, you will understand your client’s unique business questions and identify the experts who can best provide the answers. You will find and recruit new experts into our network of over 1,250,000 Guidepoint Advisors, determining which ones are best suited to speak with the client. For many of our employees, the Associate role provides a unique opportunity to put core business skills into practice, as well as gain exposure to a wide range of industries and disciplines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid position based in Manchester. While our permanent office is being finalised, you will initially work from a temporary work space and remotely. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All applicants must have the right to work in the UK.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Meet your Guidepoint Recruiter!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Initial Candidate Screen&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Meet the Guidepoint Teams!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager Interview&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Mock Assessment&amp;nbsp;(Role dependent)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Complete a simulated client request and gain more insight into the role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Mock Interview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Discuss your assessment with the Guidepoint teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Interview Process Outcome&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Team-oriented and collaborative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hard-working professionals who strive for excellence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Built-in mentorship to help you drive and improve your project management and customer service skills, to deliver excellent results for clients&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hands-on leadership to help you develop your career and provide opportunities for upward mobility within Guidepoint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Guidepoint is passionate about your career growth:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.guidepoint.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Client-Service-Promotion-Roadmap_Athens.pdf&quot;&gt;Check out our Client Service Career Trajectory.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Operate in a sales role, identifying the best experts to join our network to provide consultation for client projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Work with Project Managers to develop strategies for satisfying each client project request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Utilise LinkedIn, press releases, case studies, and the internet to identify the best experts for our clients to get their strategic or investment questions answered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify the best leads and invite them to join our network to participate in consultations with our clients&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Screen experts to determine their suitability for each specific client project and develop professional profiles to present to your clients&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Previous internship/volunteering/extracurriculars&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The right to work in the UK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Desire to work in a sales/lead generation role that is KPI and metrics-driven&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, results-oriented environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent time management and organizational skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Outgoing personality with the ability to speak with people at all professional levels&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Intellectual curiosity and desire to learn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to work both individually and as part of a team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonus and benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent medical coverage through BUPA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent professional development opportunities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Supportive culture that celebrates and rewards success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Monthly Happy Hour, Social Events, Summer Fridays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Year-round company sponsored sports and team building events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Informal work environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Employee Assistance Programs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Volunteer days&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Guidepoint:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Guidepoint is a leading research enablement platform designed to advance understanding and empower our clients’ decision-making process. Powered by innovative technology, real-time data, and hard-to-source expertise, we help our clients to turn answers into action.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Backed by a network of nearly 1.75 million experts, and Guidepoint’s 1,600 employees worldwide we inform leading organizations’ research by delivering on-demand intelligence and research on request. With Guidepoint, companies and investors can better navigate the abundance of information available today, making it both more useful and more powerful.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;At Guidepoint, our success relies on the diversity of our employees, advisors, and client base, which allows us to create connections that offer a wealth of perspectives. We are committed to upholding policies that contribute to an equitable and welcoming environment for our community, regardless of background, identity, or experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;#LI-DT1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parse Biosciences, a QIAGEN company, is a global life sciences company whose mission is to accelerate progress in human health and scientific research. Empowering researchers to perform single cell sequencing with unprecedented scale and ease, its pioneering approach has enabled groundbreaking discoveries in cancer treatment, tissue repair, stem cell therapy, kidney and liver disease, brain development, and the immune system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded based on a transformative technology invented at the University of Washington, Parse is used by over 3,000 labs across the world. Our growing portfolio of products includes Evercode Whole Transcriptome, Evercode TCR, BCR, Gene Capture, and a software tool for data analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parse Biosciences is based in Seattle, Washington&#39;s vibrant South Lake Union district, where we operate a 34,000 square foot headquarters and state-of-the-art laboratory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE POSITION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Business Development, will lead strategic business development efforts focused on expanding Parse Biosciences&#39; partnerships with pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies worldwide. Reporting to the CTO, this position will work closely with Sales, Scientific Partnerships, Product Management, Marketing, and R&amp;amp;D. This individual will identify new commercial opportunities, develop strategic customer relationships, and drive revenue growth for Parse&#39;s GigaLab services business and custom solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly customer-facing individual contributor role responsible for developing business opportunities from initial engagement through contract execution. The successful candidate will combine scientific knowledge with strong commercial acumen to build long-term strategic partnerships and expand Parse&#39;s presence within pharmaceutical research and drug discovery markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IN THIS POSITION, YOU WILL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute business development plans for key pharmaceutical and biotechnology accounts to achieve revenue growth objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, qualify, and pursue new commercial opportunities, strategic collaborations, and partnerships within the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and drug discovery markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own complex business development opportunities from initial customer engagement through proposal development, contract negotiation, and successful close.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with key stakeholders across pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and CRO organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Sales organization to develop strategic account plans and identify opportunities for expanded engagement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Director of Scientific Partnerships and internal scientific teams to develop solutions that align Parse&#39;s capabilities with customer research objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with Product Management, R&amp;amp;D, Marketing, Finance, Legal, and Operations to support customer opportunities and ensure successful execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and competitive analysis to identify emerging scientific trends, customer needs, and new market opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Parse Biosciences at scientific conferences, industry meetings, and customer events to strengthen relationships and expand business opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an accurate sales pipeline and provide regular forecasts, opportunity updates, and market insights to senior leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted commercial advisor for strategic customers while identifying opportunities for future collaboration and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FOR THIS POSITION, WE LOOK FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Life Sciences, Business, or a related field required; MBA, PhD, or related advanced degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of business development, strategic sales, or commercial experience within life sciences, biotechnology, pharmaceutical services, CROs, genomics, or related industries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success developing and closing complex commercial partnerships with pharmaceutical or biotechnology organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of pharmaceutical research, drug discovery, genomics, or related life science markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating commercial agreements and managing complex business development opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships within the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, or drug discovery community are preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated understanding of drug discovery workflows; experience supporting oncology and immunology research is highly desirable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking, analytical, negotiation, communication, and relationship-building skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across commercial, scientific, and operational teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using CRM software and Microsoft Office Suite.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed, up to approximately 40% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB CONDITIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is home office based and will require a reliable internet connection and suitable workspace to fulfill job duties effectively.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular communication and collaboration with team members will occur virtually through zoom meetings, instant messaging, and email.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel requirements: This position include regular travel to visit potential and current clients, attend conferences, and meetings or training at the company headquarters in Seattle. Candidates should have the flexibility to accommodate travel requirements as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Parse Biosciences is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;As part of our commitment to fairness and inclusion, we do not use artificial intelligence or automated systems to screen job applications. Every application is reviewed by a member of our hiring team to ensure that hiring decisions are made thoughtfully and equitably.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Revenue Accountant&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location, UK, Manchester, (Hybrid)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Inizio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio is a global partner to health and life sciences organisations, delivering specialist expertise across the product and patient journey. Through Global Finance Services (GFS), we provide high-quality, efficient and compliant finance operations that support business performance worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Global Revenue Controller, we are seeking a Senior Revenue Accountant to support revenue accounting activities within our Global Finance Services (GFS) shared services organisation, acting as a subject matter expert across complex revenue recognition, accrued and deferred revenue positions and period-end close. You will be responsible for delivering accurate and timely revenue accounting processes, ensuring compliance with revenue recognition standards, maintaining the integrity of revenue-related balance sheet accounts and supporting high-quality financial reporting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working closely with GFS RTR and OTC teams, you will perform core revenue accounting activities, support period-end close, investigate accounting issues and contribute to the effective delivery of the end-to-end Order to Cash process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Revenue Accounting &amp;amp; Financial Close&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and process revenue accounting journals and financial transactions in accordance with applicable accounting standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform reconciliations for accrued revenue, deferred revenue, contract liability and related balance sheet accounts, driving timely clearance of aged or complex reconciling items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply revenue recognition policies to assigned contracts in accordance with IFRS 15 or applicable standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile revenue ledger postings to billing system data and investigate variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead month-end, quarter-end and year-end close activities, including cut-off reviews and period-end adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate revenue accounting records, contract schedules and supporting documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with preparation of revenue reporting schedules and supporting information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate routine revenue accounting issues and escalate complex matters where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Revenue Controller in the delivery of revenue accounting, governance and financial control objectives, and share knowledge and good practice with peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GFS RTR, OTC and Group Finance teams to resolve revenue accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit activities by providing documentation and responding to information requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with accounting policies, internal controls and governance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to process improvement initiatives and operational excellence activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, data quality and revenue accounting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or equivalent professional qualification) in Accounting, Finance, Commerce or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated relevant experience in revenue accounting within a global Shared Services Centre (SSC) or Global Business Services (GBS) environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting revenue recognition, reconciliations, journal processing and month-end close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Operational Expertise&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of revenue recognition standards (IFRS 15 or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using ERP systems such as Oracle Fusion or similar accounting platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Microsoft Excel skills including lookups, pivot tables and reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding financial controls, compliance and reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate reconciliation differences, revenue recognition issues and data quality exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve routine accounting issues independently while escalating complex matters appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support improvements to accounting processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build effective relationships with Finance, Commercial teams and other internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly regarding revenue accounting queries and reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively across the shared services organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Performance, Impact &amp;amp; Ways of Working&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to accounting accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet period-end deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player focused on delivering accurate financial information and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play an important role in supporting revenue accounting quality, financial reporting accuracy and revenue recognition compliance within a global finance organisation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Accountant&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: UK, Manchester ( Hybrid)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Inizio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio is a global partner to health and life sciences organisations, delivering specialist expertise across the product and patient journey. Through Global Finance Services (GFS), we provide high-quality, efficient and compliant finance operations that support business performance worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Divisional Controller, we are seeking a Senior Accountant to lead accurate and timely period-end close activities within our Global Finance Services (GFS) shared services organisation. You will act as a subject matter expert across Record-to-Report (RTR) processes including journal preparation, balance sheet reconciliations, intercompany accounting and variance analysis while driving accounting quality, financial control and continuous improvement. Working closely with finance stakeholders, you will support governance, audit readiness and the development of junior team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Financial Accounting &amp;amp; Close&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and oversee complex accounting activities, reconciliations and financial reporting support processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key balance sheet accounts and ensure timely reconciliation and resolution of outstanding items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and sign off bank reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee intercompany accounting and resolution of differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead assigned month-end, quarter-end and year-end close activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review accounting transactions and escalate issues where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review variance analysis, providing clear commentary on movements in assigned balance sheet accounts and period-end results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review schedules and supporting information for internal and external reporting requirements, ensuring accuracy and completeness ahead of submission deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Controls&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support reporting requirements, accounting policy implementation and process changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve accounting processes, controls and reporting quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Divisional Controller in delivering accounting, governance and financial control objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and support Accountants in the execution of accounting activities and capability development; this is not a line management responsibility but carries an expectation of technical leadership and work review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or equivalent professional qualification) in Accounting, Finance, Commerce or related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–8 years&#39; progressive finance experience including financial accounting, reconciliations, intercompany accounting, close activities, audit support and financial controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a global Shared Services Centre (SSC) or Global Business Services (GBS) environment is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Operational Expertise&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP experience (Oracle Fusion or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Microsoft Excel skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong accounting standards, financial reporting and balance sheet management knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of internal controls and SOX or equivalent governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting process improvement or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex reconciliations, intercompany disputes and accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply judgement to non-routine transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvements and control enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build effective relationships with Finance, Tax, Treasury, Audit and Divisional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical accounting matters clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Performance, Impact &amp;amp; Ways of Working&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and strong organisational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, proactive and committed to continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play a key role in delivering high-quality financial reporting and strengthening accounting controls across Global Finance Services while supporting continuous improvement and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialized industries, their employees, and their customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build, and grow great companies worldwide, helping them modernize through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world. Banyan is Great Place to Work Certified, a five-time Inc. 5000 honoree, and a top 10 company on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 and headquartered in Atlanta, Banyan operates more than 100 portfolio companies across North America, the UK, EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialised industries, their employees, and their customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build, and grow great companies worldwide, helping them modernise through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world. Banyan is a Great Place to Work Certified company, a five-time Inc. 5000 honoree, and a top-10 company on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 and headquartered in Atlanta, Banyan operates more than 100 portfolio companies across North America, the UK, the EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WIZE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WIZE is the leading all-in-one Portfolio Management System for Swiss boutique wealth managers, External Asset Managers, and family offices. Founded in Geneva in 2010, WIZE has earned a trusted position in a relationship-driven market through deep product capability and a differentiated back-office outsourcing service that competitors have not replicated. The company operates on a highly recurring subscription model, holds a strong position within its vertical, and is in excellent operating shape. WIZE is now entering its first chapter of international ownership under Banyan Software, combining more than fifteen years of product depth and client trust with the operational and AI expertise of a global software group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join WIZE directly as Managing Director,&amp;nbsp; United Kingdom, reporting to the CEO of WIZE, with responsibility for establishing and growing the UK business. This is a value-creation mandate, not a turnaround. . You will take the business into a new market, with the United Kingdom as the primary prize. The product has to remain the primary competitive advantage, the recurring revenue base has to be protected, and the opportunity to create structural distance through AI is real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the UK client and partner relationships, build the commercial motion from the ground up, and partner with the CEO and product and technology leader to ensure the platform addresses the needs of the UK market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have substantial authority over the execution of the agreed UK strategy. Key commercial development decisions, including market positioning, target segments, pricing, partnerships, resource allocation, and major commercial commitments, will be decided jointly with the CEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will do this with the long-term backing of a permanent-capital owner, free from the pressure to flip the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Revenue Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the foundation of the UK subsidiary and work closely with the CEO to define WIZE&#39;s expansion into the UK market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the execution of WIZE&#39;s UK strategy, market positioning, and competitive response in the wealth management software market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive UK revenue and ARR growth with direct accountability across new customer acquisition, expansion, pricing execution, and the development of recurring revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute the UK go-to-market motion from the ground up: local presence, bank and partner relationships, and a repeatable pipeline where little exists today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary executive relationship owner for key UK clients, bank partners, and influencers, ensuring high levels of client satisfaction, retention, and contract renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deepen strategic partnerships across private banks, discretionary fund managers, and the wider UK wealth management ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate client needs and proactively identify opportunities to expand the company&#39;s footprint within existing UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify AI-driven opportunities to reposition the product and create durable competitive distance within the WealthTech vertical, working with the CEO and product and technology leader to assess and prioritise them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the needs of the UK market in product roadmap discussions, ensuring that market feedback reflects the needs of boutique wealth managers and the competitive dynamics of the Portfolio Management Systems market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a credible AI roadmap. AI must be embedded as a genuine operational and product advantage, not a roadmap line item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-first product thinking, identifying where automation, predictive insights, and intelligent workflows create durable differentiation for UK clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the CEO and CPTO so that the roadmap, packaging, and pricing tiers align tightly with UK commercial needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather structured feedback from UK prospects, clients, and partners and translate it into clear commercial and product recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement the UK commercial development strategy jointly with the CEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the UK financial performance, budgeting, and resource allocation to ensure sustainable profitability. Prepare and manage the UK commercial budget and resource plan, subject to approval by the CEO and Chief Revenue Officer, to ensure sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage risk across operations, contracts, and market dynamics; respond decisively to changes in the competitive or regulatory landscape&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing UK sales team, elevating talent density and making hard calls on underperformance with speed and directness, while protecting the trust-based culture that makes WIZE what it is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish decision rights, execution cadences, and accountability frameworks that enable the business to sustain higher growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and proactively with the CEO on business performance, strategic priorities, pipeline development, and market conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with WIZE&#39;s Geneva-based product, technology, implementation, client service, compliance, and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Managing Director we are looking for is a commercially-led WealthTech operator with deep roots in the UK wealth management software market who leads with an AI-first mindset and is energised by the opportunity to create real, lasting business value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have personally owned a revenue number, built a commercial motion where none existed, and opened a new geography from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have held senior commercial responsibility at a software company serving wealth managers, private banks, or asset managers, with a track record of treating product as a primary strategic lever, closing complex, relationship-driven deals at a senior level, and leading your organisation through at least one meaningful inflexion point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You proactively reposition ahead of market pressure, make difficult commercial and talent decisions for the long-term health of the business, and understand how to grow recurring revenue and protect the retention that sustains durability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a value-creating enterprise SaaS leader who sees AI not as a feature but as a structural advantage embedded in how they sell, operate, and create enduring competitive distance for the businesses they lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications for Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owned the P&amp;amp;L or revenue number of a B2B SaaS, FinTech, or vertical software business, with direct accountability for revenue growth, retention, and margin expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10+ years of senior commercial leadership at a software or technology company, including direct responsibility for selling to, managing, or delivering to wealth managers, private banks, or asset managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in wealth management software or Portfolio Management Systems, or adjacent FinTech / WealthTech. Experience at a direct competitor carries immediate credibility with prospects and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the UK wealth management ecosystem (private banks, discretionary fund managers, IFAs, and External Asset Managers) and existing relationships with key buyers and influencers. Ideally, UK-based or strongly tied to the UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built a go-to-market motion in a new geography: hiring local talent, establishing partnerships, and opening a market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led an organisation through a meaningful inflexion point, such as a competitive situation, building a business from scratch, pricing repositioning, or commercial professionalisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI conviction: shipped product capability, embedded operational tooling, or led sustained AI experimentation with clear conviction about where it creates durable value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable building and leading a local commercial operation within a company of roughly 30 to 80 people in an investor-backed setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to operate entrepreneurially while working within a jointly agreed strategy and governance framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English is essential. French is a significant advantage given the Geneva headquarters and Swiss relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in the UK, ideally within reach of London, and able to commit to regular on-site presence in Geneva.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
